  #line-at(108.05pt, 414.62pt, "In this work, we show that expanded graphite can lead to remarkable increase in thermal ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 435.15pt, "conductivity of polyetherimide composites prepared via the approach of solvent casting. Expanded ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 455.9pt, "graphite has a highly porous structure with interconnected graphitic walls as seen in the SEM ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 476.65pt, "image of expanded graphite in air in Fig. 1f. The graphitic sheets form a continuous network over ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 497.4pt, "long length scales, allowing efficient conduction of heat. The approach of solvent casting offers ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 518.17pt, "the advantage of preserving this porous structure of expanded graphite as seen in the Field ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 538.67pt, "Emission Environmental Scanning Electron Microscopy (FE-ESEM) images of expanded ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 559.42pt, "graphite, while it is embedded in the polymer composite, in Figs. 1h, i and k.  Comparison of Figs. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 580.17pt, "1f (showing EG in air) and Figs. 1h, i and k (showing EG in the composite), clearly show that the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 600.95pt, "porous structure of EG is retained within the composite. This is due to the use of solvent casting, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 621.7pt, "which does not exert large forces on expanded graphite, preserving its porous structure, unlike ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 642.2pt, "micro-compounding where large shear forces distort this structure. Such a porous structure gets ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 662.95pt, "infused with the dissolved polymer during the casting process resulting in a highly conductive ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 683.72pt, "interpenetrating network of graphene and polymer.  ")
]

