  #line-at(72.025pt, 83.28pt, "GnPs  and polymer then restricts the enhancement achievable through use of graphene ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 104.03pt, "nanoplatelets. These results highlight the large advantage of expanded graphite over graphene ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 124.8pt, "nanoplatelets in enhancing composite thermal conductivity.  ")
  #line-at(108.05pt, 145.3pt, "We further investigated the effect of sonication parameters used during composite ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 166.05pt, "preparation on ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(143.55pt, 166.05pt, "k")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(148.83pt, 166.05pt, " enhancement.  Figs. 3c and d show that lower sonication time and amplitude leads ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 186.8pt, "to higher thermal conductivity of EG/PEID composite. To understand the effect of sonication ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 207.58pt, "parameters on structural integrity of EG, we performed FE-SEM analysis. As the porous ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 228.33pt, "interpenetrating network has beneficial impact on thermal conductivity enhancement (shown in ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 248.83pt, "fig 4a-d), high resolution images are obtained to visualize the effect of sonication time on this ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 269.58pt, "porous network structure (Fig 5a, b). The image of 10 wt% EG/PEID composite (Fig. 5a and b) ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 290.35pt, "prepared with 3min sonication time at 20% amplitude shows an absence of porous structure within ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 311.1pt, "the composite suggesting that longer sonication time causes the porous structure to be damaged. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 331.85pt, "FE-SEM image of 10wt% GnP/PEID composite are also presented here in Figs. 5c & d.   ")
  #line-at(108.05pt, 352.35pt, "While above images show the expanded graphite embedded in polymer, we also show ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 373.12pt, "expanded graphite before it is embedded into the polymer in Figs. 5e & f. These images show that ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 393.87pt, "fragile, porous graphite is broken into nanosheets after 3 minutes sonication time whereas 40 sec ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 414.62pt, "sonication time has negligible effect on EG filler structure. Short time sonication thus offers the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 435.15pt, "advantage of preserving the structure of expanded graphite, while also allowing uniform dispersion ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 455.9pt, "into the polymer matrix.  ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 476.65pt, "       In the next section, we compare measured ")
