  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 83.28pt, "conductivity is found to be a due to a network of continuous graphene sheets over long length ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 104.03pt, "scales achieved through ")
  #line-at(196.08pt, 104.03pt, "solvent casting technique which preserves the interconnected porous ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 124.8pt, "structure of expanded graphite within the composite. Even at bends/turns in graphene sheets in ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 145.3pt, "such a network, the sheets are covalently bonded which minimizes the interfacial thermal ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 166.05pt, "resistance at junctions, enhancing heat transfer. Overall, the resulting structure allows highly ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 186.8pt, "efficient heat conduction over long length scales along the continuous graphitic sheets. This results ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 207.58pt, "in the observed high thermal conductivity of the composite through use of EG. Thermal ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 228.33pt, "conductivity of EG/PEID composite is also found to dramatically exceed that of graphene-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 248.83pt, "nanoplatelet (GnP)/PEID composites by 572% for 10 wt% filler composition. At low filler loading, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 269.58pt, "GnPs are well separated by polymer, and the resulting high graphene-polymer interfacial thermal ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 290.35pt, "resistance, results in low effective GnP/PEID thermal conductivity. Presented results highlight the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 311.1pt, "advantage of expanded graphite in enhancing thermal conductivity of polymer composites, and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 331.85pt, "can lead to novel avenues for achieving efficient thermal management in a wide array of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 352.35pt, "technologies.  ")
